# CODEOWNERS — Tech Inventory
#
# Single-operator repository. `@briandenicola` owns everything; this file exists
# so ownership is stated rather than assumed, and so a future second contributor
# inherits working routing instead of a placeholder.
#
# Practical limits, stated plainly (do not treat this file as a control):
#   * GitHub cannot request a review from the author of a PR. With one
#     maintainer, code-owner review is unenforceable, so branch protection is
#     recommended WITHOUT `require_code_owner_reviews`
#     (specs/004-agentic-development-foundation/t105-governance-evidence.md §4).
#   * Until branch protection exists, CODEOWNERS auto-requests reviews at most;
#     it blocks nothing.
#   * Every path below is verified to exist. Do not add a pattern for a path
#     that does not exist — a rule that can never match is noise pretending to
#     be governance. (The former `deploy/` entry was exactly that and is removed.)

